Infovox 230 -> NVDA add-on
==========================

This repository contains material under several different licenses. Read this
file before redistributing.

1. Add-on code (the parts written for this project)
---------------------------------------------------
The NVDA synthesizer driver, the 32-bit host, the Sx32w dongle-emulator stub,
and the tooling/tests -- i.e. everything under `nvda-infovox230/addon/synthDrivers/infovox230.py`,
`nvda-infovox230/host/`, `nvda-infovox230/sx32w_stub/`, and `nvda-infovox230/tools/`
-- are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2, to match NVDA
and its add-ons.

    This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it
    under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free
    Software Foundation; either version 2 of the License, or (at your option)
    any later version.

    This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT
    ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or
    FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the GNU General Public License for
    more details.

The full text of the GPL version 2 is available at:
    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt

2. The Infovox 230 engine, rule sets, and voice data
----------------------------------------------------
The Infovox 230 text-to-speech engine (`Ivx230nt.dll`), its language rule sets
(`*.IVX`, `darules.dll`), and the voice/speaker definitions originate from Telia
Promotor / Babel-Infovox AB. Both companies are defunct; the software is
included here with the maintainer's stated permission to use and modify it
freely. The engine binary in this repository has been
patched (see `nvda-infovox230/ARCHITECTURE.md`) to run without its original
hardware dongle and license manager.

3. Third-party components in the original installer
---------------------------------------------------
The preserved original installer (`Infovox230v2_2complete.exe`) and its
extracted contents include third-party components that are NOT covered by the
above and remain under their own respective licenses -- notably Microsoft
runtime libraries (`MFC40.DLL`, `mfc42.dll`, `msvcrt40.dll`, `OLEPRO32.DLL`),
CrypKey licensing files, and InstallShield installer components. They are
included only as part of the original, already-publicly-archived installer
materials and are not relicensed here.
